[profiles.guide]
notes = '''Hold {select} and {start} together to pause the gyro while you reposition the controller. Hold {start} to switch the gyro off or on, and hold {r3} to recenter it.
{start} (Escape) opens the game's menu and closes the other screens.
{south} picks up, uses and drinks blood bags or pours them; hold {south} to sprint. {east} jumps and {l3} toggles crouch. {west} reloads and {north} switches the flashlight on and off.
{rt} fires or attacks, and {lt} aims; the right stick turns more finely while it's held. {left} and {right} step through what you carry.
Infected: {lb} transforms when the lights go out. Hold {select} for the player list, and hold {up} to talk on voice chat if you use push-to-talk. Text chat needs typing: open the on-screen keyboard with {guide} + {west}.
These keys are written from memory and not checked in the game (transform, flashlight, voice and the item keys especially); compare them with Options → Controls and change the buttons here to match. The executable rule's name comes from Discord's game list and isn't checked. Deceit uses Easy Anti-Cheat, which sees the pad as an ordinary keyboard and mouse. The gyro's full turn is a guess, not measured: turn in place and adjust it until a full turn of the controller turns you around once.'''

